// Title: IIS WebServer Log Deletion via CommandLine Utilities
// ID: 0649be4a-aeb0-45b0-b89e-7f1668f6d9c0
// Status: experimental
// Level: medium
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2025-09-02
// Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1070
// Description: Detects attempts to delete Internet Information Services (IIS) log files via command line utilities, which is a common defense evasion technique used by attackers to cover their tracks.
// Threat actors often abuse vulnerabilities in web applications hosted on IIS servers to gain initial access and later delete IIS logs to evade detection.
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "del ") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "erase ") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "rm ") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "remove-item ") OR where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "rmdir "))) AND (where(CommandLine ICONTAINS "\\inetpub\\logs\\")) AND (((where(Image IENDSWITH "\\cmd.exe") OR where(Image IENDSWITH "\\powershell_ise.exe") OR where(Image IENDSWITH "\\powershell.exe") OR where(Image IENDSWITH "\\pwsh.exe"))) OR ((where(OriginalFileName = "cmd.exe") OR where(OriginalFileName = "powershell.exe") OR where(OriginalFileName = "powershell_ise.exe") OR where(OriginalFileName = "pwsh.dll")))))
